WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.508
<v Narrator>I open Homework Helper.

2
00:00:03.866 --> 00:00:05.919
<v Tutor>Hi there! I am your Homework Helper,

3
00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:07.972
<v Tutor>and I am so excited to work with you.

4
00:00:07.972 --> 00:00:09.805
<v Tutor>You can type a question, draw it,

5
00:00:09.805 --> 00:00:13.178
<v Tutor>or just upload a photo of your assignment to get started.

6
00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:14.864
<v Tutor>What are we working on today?

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.975
<v Narrator>I type a math question and send it.

8
00:00:22.964 --> 00:00:25.105
<v Tutor>To check if that is correct,

9
00:00:25.105 --> 00:00:27.537
<v Tutor>we can plug 5 into the equation.

10
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:32.109
<v Tutor>If we replace x with 5, the equation becomes 3 times 5 plus 5.

11
00:00:32.109 --> 00:00:35.417
<v Tutor>Since 3 times 5 is 15, and 15 plus 5 equals 20,

12
00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:37.265
<v Tutor>your answer is correct!

13
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.940
<v Narrator>Now I upload a science homework question.

14
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.012
<v Narrator>I ask for a short explanation.

15
00:00:52.864 --> 00:00:56.649
<v Tutor>Since the density of ice is lower than the density of liquid water,

16
00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:57.981
<v Tutor>the ice cube will float.

17
00:00:57.981 --> 00:01:00.100
<v Tutor>This happens because less dense objects

18
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.466
<v Tutor>rise to the top of more dense liquids.

19
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.634
<v Narrator>I review the answer, then end the call.
